","Protein-binding domains, such as SH2, SH3, and ligand binding domains, play a crucial role in the regulation of various cellular processes, including those involved in the development and progression of neurodegenerative diseases. These domains are crucial for the formation of protein-protein interactions, which can be targeted for therapeutic intervention in diseases involving excitotoxicity.

