1. **Convert pounds to kilograms:**
   \[
   \text{kilograms} = \frac{\text{pounds}}{2.205} = \frac{32 \text{ lbs}}{2.205} \approx 14.42 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. **Calculate the loading dose:**
   \[
   \text{Loading dose} = 20 \text{ mg/kg} \times 14.42 \text{ kg} = 288.4 \text{ mg}
   \]

3. **Calculate the infusion time:**
   \[
   \text{Infjection time} = \frac{\text{Loading dose}}{\text{Injection rate}} = \frac{288.4 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 576.8 \text{ min}
   \]

   The dosage is \(\boxed{577 \text{ minutes}}\).
