<GROUND_TRUTH>
When the diet contains an excess of carbohydrates, glucose is converted into fatty acids. This occurs because the body stores excess glucose as fat for long-term energy storage. The process involves glycolysis to break down glucose into pyruvate, which is then converted into acetyl-CoA. Acetyl-CoA serves as the precursor for fatty acid synthesis. Thus, $\boxed{\text{Excess carbohydrates in the diet}}$ lead to the conversion of glucose to fatty acids.
