\]
The complex `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` dissociates into `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]⁺` and `Cl₂⁻`. The `Cl₂⁻` further dissociates into `Cl⁻` and `Cl⁻`. Thus, the overall dissociation is:
\[
[\text{Pt(NH}_3\text{)}_4\text{Cl}_2]^+ \text{Cl}^- \rightarrow [\text{Pt(NH}_3\text{)}_4\text{Cl}_2]^+ + 2\text{Cl}^-
\]
Thus, the complex `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]Cl2` dissociates into `[Pt(NH3)4Cl2]⁺` and `2Cl⁻`. The number of chloride ions produced is `2`.

