Determine the system reliability function \( R_S(t) \) for a non-repairable system with independent components, where the system's reliability structure is:
a) A serial structure  
b) A parallel structure  
c) A combination of serial and parallel structures<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","a) **Series System:**  
   - In a series system, the system fails if only one component fails.  
   - The reliability function \( R_S(t) \) is the product of the individual component reliutions \( R_i(t) \), where \( i \) ranges from 1 to \( n \), and \( n \) is the number of components.  
   - For a series system with \( n \) independent components with reliability functions \( R_1(t) \), \( R_2(t) \), \( R_3(t) \), \( R_4(t) \), \( R_5(t) \), \( R_6(t) \), \( R_7(t) \), \( R_8(t) \), \( R_9(t) \), \( R_{10}(t) \), the reliability function is:  
     \[
     R_S(t) = R_1(t) \times R_2(t) \times R_3(t) \times R_4(t) \times R_5(t) \times R_6(t) \times R_7(t) \times R_8(t) \times R_9(t) \times R_{10}(t)
     \]  
   - For a general series system with \( n \) components:  
     \[
     R_S(t) = \prod_{i=1}^{n} R_i(t)
     \]  

b) **Parallel System:**  
