\]
where \( I \) is the current, \( \mu_0 \) is the permeability of free space, \( a \) and \( b \) are the inner and outer radii of the coaxial shell, \( \theta \) is the angle from the axis, and \( \hat{n} \) is the unit vector in the direction of \( S \).

\[
\boxed{S = \frac{I \mu_0}{2\pi} \frac{a^2}{b^2 - a^2} \sin \theta \, \hat{n}}
