(G ∪ P) = 90 - 35
(G ∪ P) = 55

Now we can find B:

B = G + P - (G ∪ P)
B = 50 + 40 - 55
B = 90 - 55
B = 35

So, there are $\boxed{35}$  houses that have both a two-car garage and an in-the-ground swimming pool.
