","The forward amplifier gain is \( A_v = 100 \). The feedback gain is \( m_v = 0.1 \). The closed-loop voltage gain is given by:
\[
A_{vf} = \frac{A_v}{1 - m_v}
\]
Substituting the given values:
\[
A_{fw} = \frac{100}{1 - 0.1} = \frac{100}{0.9} \approx 111.11 \text{ V}
\]
The amplifier's gain decreases by 6 dB due to aging. The new forward gain \( A'_v \) is:
\[
A'_v = \frac{A_v}{10^{6/10}} = \frac{100}{10^{0.6}} \approx \frac{100}{3.16} \approx 31.72 \text{ V}
\]
The new closed-loop voltage gain \( A'_{vf} \) is:
\[
A'_{fw} = \frac{A'_v}{1 - m_y} = \frac{31.72}{1 - 0.1} = \frac{31.72}{0.9} \approx 35.24 \text{ V}
\]
The percentage change in the closed-loop gain is:
\[
\text{Percentage change} = \left( \frac{A'_{vf} - A_{vf}}{A_{vf}} \right) \times 100 = \left( \frac{35.24 - 111.11}{111.11} \right) \times 100 \approx \left( \frac{-75.87}{111.11} \right) \times 100 \approx -68.3\%
\]
