\[
E_f^2 = \gamma_f^2 c^4 \quad \text{and} \quad E_i^2 = \gamma_i^2 c^4
\]

Substituting these into the expression for \( Q^2 \):

\[
Q^2 = \gamma_f^2 c^4 - \gamma_i^2 c^4 - \left( \mathbf{p}_f \cdot \mathbf{p}_f \right) + \left( \mathbf{p}_i \cdot \mathbf{p}_i \right)
\]

The dot products of the position components are:

\[
\mathbf{p}_f \cdot \mathbf{p}_f = p_f^2 \quad \text{and} \quad \mathbf{p}_i \cdot \mathbf{p}_i = p_i^2
\]

Thus:

\[
Q^2 = \gamma_f^2 c^4 - \gamma_i^2 c^4 - p_f^2 + p_i^2
\]

