At the beginning, the initial moles of acetic acid (CH₃COOH) and ethyl alcohol (C₂H₅OH) are both 1 mole. At equilibrium, the moles of unreacted acetic acid are 0.333 moles.

1. Calculate the moles of acetic acid that reacted:
Initial moles of CH₃COOH = 1 mole
Moles of unreacted CH₃COOH = 0.333 moles
Moles of CH₃COOH reacted = 1 - 0.333 = 0.667 moles

2. Since the reaction is 1:1, the moles of ethanol (C₂H₅OH) that reacted are also 0.667 moles:
Initial moles of C₂H₅OH = 1 mole
Moles of CH₃COOH reacted = 0.667 moles
Moles of C₂H₅OH reacted = 0.667 moles
Moles of unreacted C₂H₅OH = 1 - 0.667 = 0.333 moles

