\]

where:
- \( F = 3600 \, \text{N} \) (gravitational force)
- \( G = 8.87 \times 10^{-5} \, \text{N m}^2/\text{kg}^2 \) (gravitational constant)
- \( m_0 = 6 \times 10^{23} \, \text{kg} \) (mass of the Earth)
- \( r = 10^5 \, \text{m} \) (radius of the Earth)

Substituting the given values:

\[
3600 = \frac{8.87 \times 10^{-5} \times m_0^2}{r^2}
\]

Solving for \( m \):
\[
m = \frac{r^2 \times F}{G \times m_0}
\]

