2H₂(g) + O₂(g) → 2H₂O(l)

We are given the standard Gibbs free energy of formation of water (ΔG°(H₂O)) as -237.1 kJ/mol. The standard Gibbs free energy of formation for hydrogen gas (H₂) and oxygen gas (O₂) is zero, as they are in their standard states.

