- \( \lambda \) is the wavelength of the radiation in meters.
- \( h \) is Planck's constant (\( 6.626 \times 10^{-34} \, \text{J s} \)).

This equation represents the spectral energy density, which is the power emitted per unit area per unit wavelength. 

