The coefficient of restitution \( e \) is given by:
\[
e = \frac{\text{Velocity of rebound}}{\text{Velocity of impact}} = \frac{v_{\text{out}}}{v_{\text{in}}}
\]
Given \( e = \frac{1}{3} \), the ratio of the velocity of the block after the collision to the velocity of the block before the collision is \( \frac{1}{3} \).

The kinetic energy of the ball before the collision is:
\[
K_{\text{initial}} = \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{in}}^2
\]
The kinetic energy of the ball after the collision is:
\[
K_{\text{final}} = \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{out}}^2
\]
Since \( e = \frac{v_{\text{out}}}{v_{\text{in}}} = \frac{1}{3} \), we have:
\[
v_{\text{out}} = \frac{1}{3} v_{\text{in}}
\]
Thus, the coefficient energy after the collision is:
\[
K_{\text{final}} = \frac{1}{2} m \left( \frac{1}{3} v_{\text{in}} \right)^2 = \frac{1}{2} m \cdot \frac{1}{9} v_{\text{in}}^2 = \frac{1}{9} \left( \frac{1}{2} m v_{\text{in}}^2 \right) = \frac{1}{9} K_{\text{initial}}
\]
The fraction of kinetic energy lost is:
\[
\text{Fraction lost} = 1 - \frac{K_{\text{final}}}{K_{\text{initial}}} = 1 - \frac{1}{9} = \frac{8}{9}
