","(a) The electric force \(F\) on the proton is given by:  
\[
F = qE = (1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C})(500 \, \text{N/C}) = 8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}
\]  
Using Newton's second law, the acceleration \(a\) is:  
\[
a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{8.0 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} = 4.8 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2
\]  
The magnitude of the acceleration is \(\boxed{4.8 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2}\).

(b) Using the kinematic equation for acceleration:  
\[
v = u + at
\]  
where \(v = 35,000 \, \text{m/s}\), \(u = 0 \, \text{m/s}\) (since the proton starts from rest), and \(a = 4.8 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2\), we solve for \(t\):  
\[
t = \frac{v - u}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s} - 0 \, \text{m/s}}{4.8 \times 10^{10} \, \text{m/s}^2} = \boxed{7.2 \times 10^{-4} \, \text{s}}
\]  

