This reaction occurs at the anode (left side of the battery). The anode is made of lead (Pb), and the anode is in contact with a solution of sulfuric acid (H₂SO₄) and lead sulfate (PbSO₄). During discharge, the lead (Pb) reacts with the lead sulfate (PbSO₄) and hydrogen ions (H⁺) from the sulfuric acid, forming more lead sulfate (PbSO₄) and hydrogen gas (H₂).  

